Start at £1,950 a month for your first two clients. When you take on client three or four, move to £2,450. By client five or six, £2,950 is a fair and defensible number. You are not discounting for early clients out of generosity - you are building proof and rhythm. The clients who come in early get the lowest rate and they keep it. Everyone after pays the current rate. Each time you raise it, the next prospect anchors to a higher number without you having to justify the gap. Do not wait until you feel ready to raise it. Raise it when the next client comes in.

